; form-find-run.fk — the form-find SERVICE: the source tree indexed and resident, answering the agent wire through a spool directory.
; The host's manager runs this (docs/launchd/earth.hati.form-find.plist: launchd KeepAlive starts it again if it dies or is stopped); the
; body never begins it. It walks the tree once (source-tree.bml, every .gitignore honoured), holds each text file, a definition index,
; the import edges, the band headers and a trigram posting set, writes service.pid once, then rests on host_watch over the spool
; (FORM_FIND_SPOOL, default /tmp/form-find/<UID>) and the memory notes: an ask wakes it and is answered as ans.<n>.json, a note written,
; added or removed wakes it and the notes' index is rewritten. Nothing runs on a clock. Every query first stats each file and lists each
; directory whose mtime moved, so the index follows the tree on demand. A file named `stop` in the spool ends the loop (launchd then
; starts the next); the operator takes the service away
; with launchctl bootout. The `path` verb (form-path.bml: an XPath-shaped query over the files' nodes) is taught to the same index.
; Proof: form/form-stdlib/tests/form-find-band.fk (the loop's one-request function and the spool, called in process),
; form/form-stdlib/tests/form-path-band.fk (the path verb).
; preflight-exec: forbidden
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/bml/form-path.bml
(do
    (fpa-run)
    0)
